{{/*
  beads-issues/shared/loop-driver-guidelines-common — the 4 "## Guidelines"
  bullets shared by all three loop-driver-shaped prompts (loop-fixing-bug,
  loop-implementing-feature, publish-post): Live state / Decide
  autonomously / Silent unless it matters / Log a concise delta.

  Callers pass the caller-specific milestone list spliced into the "Silent
  unless it matters" bullet:

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/loop-driver-guidelines-common" (dict
          "MilestoneList" "phase dispatched, fixed, blocked/deferred, or final stop"
      ) }}

  Parameters:
    MilestoneList — comma-separated list of the milestones that warrant a
                    `mitto_ui_notify` call on scheduled runs. Spliced into
                    the parenthetical at the end of the "Silent unless it
                    matters" bullet.
    Target        — effective bead ID; when supplied, the driver writes the
                    canonical execution-state block in the ticket notes.

  The output is column-0 text (matches the existing beads-issues/shared/*
  fragments' convention). The caller's YAML `content: |` scalar's own
  indentation is applied by the YAML loader before the template engine
  runs, so this fragment renders at the same visible indent as the
  caller's surrounding bullets — no double-indentation.
*/ -}}
- **Live state only.** Always re-read labels via `bd show --json` at the start of the
  run; never assume labels from a prior run or from `Item.*`.
- **Decide autonomously; never guess.** The only time you must not proceed is when
  something is genuinely unclear/unsolvable without the user — then use Step 4.
- **Silent unless it matters.** On scheduled runs, `mitto_ui_notify` only for
  meaningful milestones ({{ .MilestoneList }}).
- **Log a concise delta/verdict** with `bd comment`; skip no-op runs even when
  you stay silent in the UI.
